<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">16 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 16 November, from 1093 to 1988.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/scotland" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/scotland.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1093 <span class="tih-ago">933 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Queen Margaret of Scotland dies</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Margaret, wife of Malcolm III, died in Edinburgh Castle days after learning that her husband and eldest son had been killed at Alnwick. Celebrated for her piety and church reform, she was canonised in 1250.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1532 <span class="tih-ago">494 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pizarro captures the Inca ruler Atahualpa at Cajamarca</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Francisco Pizarro's force of fewer than 200 men ambushed Atahualpa's retinue in the square of Cajamarca, killing thousands. Holding the Inca ruler captive gave the Spanish leverage over a vast empire.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro">Francisco Pizarro</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1776 <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The British capture Fort Washington on Manhattan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British and Hessian troops stormed Fort Washington, the last American stronghold on Manhattan, and took about 2,800 prisoners. Washington's army retreated across New Jersey.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-nations.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1945 <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">UNESCO's constitution is signed in London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Delegates of 37 countries signed the constitution of the United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization. It promotes cooperation in education, science and culture and lists World Heritage Sites.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pakistan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1988 <span class="tih-ago">38 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Benazir Bhutto's party wins Pakistan's general election</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Pakistan Peoples Party, led by Benazir Bhutto, won the most seats in the first open election in over a decade. Weeks later she became the first woman to lead a Muslim-majority democracy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a></div></div></li></ol>
